sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (ADR 0248, option A chosen 2026-11-07): every publication renders the complete private DNS from the Gateway database, and one Ansible phase writes one dnsmasq configuration on the vpn Node. Shared by Route, Node, Cluster and role kinds.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: none · shared step of Route, Node, Cluster and role kinds
  %% kind: dns.publish
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as VPN Node<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Render all private DNS<br/>one revision, three files
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads every Route, Node, Cluster and role holder from the database
  %%> - renders the complete state, never a piece of it
  %%> - takes the revision in the same transaction that reads the rows
  %%> Result:
  %%> - `orbit.conf`, `orbit.hosts` and `orbit.servers` as text, and the revision
  %%> Why:
  %%> - each publication is a whole state, so two parallel publications cannot lose each other's change
  %%> - every caller gets the same answer
  GW->>SW: Start run with the render<br/>child workflow dns-publish
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the owning kind (Route, Node, Cluster or role change) starts this step in its own run
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the render (TLDs, records, listen address) and the revision
  %%> - the address and SSH host keys of the VPN Node
  Note over SW: Write the intent
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the render and the connection of the Node to a 0600 file in the run folder, and ships the playbook
  SW->>N: Run the DNS phase<br/>ansible-playbook dns-publish
  %%> How:
  %%> - one Ansible phase reads, changes and checks the Node in one run
  %%> - a Swamp worker reaches the Node over SSH
  %%> - the phase holds the Node's dnsmasq lock from the first read to the last write
  alt revision is newer than installed
    %% path: newer-revision
    Note over N: Validate the files<br/>dnsmasq --test
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks the new files in a temporary folder before anything is replaced
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - nothing is installed and the phase fails with `dns.config_invalid`
    Note over N: Install changed files
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - saves the installed files as the last good set, then replaces only the files whose content changed, each in one rename
    alt orbit.conf is unchanged
      %% path: reload
      Note over N: Reload dnsmasq<br/>SIGHUP
      %%> Why:
      %%> - dnsmasq reads the hosts and servers files again on SIGHUP, so an exact Route change drops no query
      %%> - unchanged means equal to the copy dnsmasq last started with
    else orbit.conf changed
      %% path: restart
      Note over N: Restart dnsmasq
      %%> When:
      %%> - a TLD is added, changed or removed; dnsmasq reads `orbit.conf` only at start
      %%> - also when an earlier restart failed after the file was installed
    end
    Note over N: Check the answers<br/>dig on the VPN address
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks the running dnsmasq for the reserved names and one name per TLD
    %%> - for each exact Route: the A answer, AAAA gives NODATA, and a child name is forwarded
    %%> - fails the phase when an answer differs from the render
    Note over N: Record the revision
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - writes `orbit.revision` last, so a failed run leaves the old revision and a rerun repairs it
  else same or older revision
    %% path: superseded
    Note over N: Skipped — superseded<br/>dns.revision_superseded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a newer publication already wrote a state that includes this change
    %%> - the files stay as they are and the phase still succeeds
  end
  alt files installed and answers match
    %% path: succeeded
    N-->>SW: Phase result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the installed revision and whether dnsmasq reloaded, restarted or stayed
  else validation or check fails
    %% path: failed
    Note over N: Restore last good files
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - runs only when the check failed after the install; puts the last good files back and reloads or restarts dnsmasq
    %%> - a `dns.config_invalid` refusal installed nothing, so there is nothing to restore
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0
    %%> When:
    %%> - dnsmasq refuses the files (`dns.config_invalid`), SSH fails, or an answer differs from the render (`dns.check_failed`)
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - the phase restores the last good files and reloads or restarts dnsmasq; a rerun renders and writes the whole state again
  end
  Note over SW: Report the result
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - prints the phase's `result.json` (`{revision, dnsmasq}`, or `{error_code}`), also after a failed phase
  %%> - this is the terminal step the Gateway reads
  Note over SW: Remove the run folder
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - deletes the intent and the shipped playbook, whatever happened
  alt files installed and answers match
    %% path: recorded
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the owning kind continues with its next step
  else validation or check fails
    %% path: refused
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and the `error_code` that Report the result printed
    Note over GW: Mark the owner failed
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the owning command again after fixing the cause
  end
